# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# This file is copied verbatim into dist/ by the Astro build, which is where
# Cloudflare Pages reads it from. It is the only place response headers are
# set: the site is static, there is no SSR adapter and no Pages Function, so
# nothing else is in the request path.
#
# The rule below is `/*`, so it applies to every response the project serves,
# including 404.html.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE CSP HASHES ARE BUILD OUTPUT AND THEY GO STALE.
#
# Astro emits two inline <script> blocks and one inline <style> on every page:
# the `client:load` directive loader, the <astro-island> custom element that
# hydrates MobileMenu.vue, and `astro-island,astro-slot,astro-static-slot
# {display:contents}`. There is no `src` to point at and, on a static host,
# no request-time nonce to issue, so the only way to allow exactly those three
# and nothing else is to hash them.
#
# The three hashes are of the current build. An Astro upgrade that changes one
# byte of that runtime changes its hash, the browser refuses the script, and
# the island never hydrates: the mobile menu stops opening, which is the only
# navigation a desktop user has at 400% zoom. That failure is silent in the
# page and loud only in the console.
#
# tests/headers.spec.ts recomputes all three from dist/ and fails when this
# file and the build have drifted. Do not hand-edit a hash; re-run the suite,
# take the values from the failure message, and check the diff is only the
# Astro runtime.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HSTS IS SET SHORT, AND WITHOUT includeSubDomains OR preload, ON PURPOSE.
#
# max-age=86400 is one day. It is the one header here that a browser keeps
# after the response is gone: for as long as max-age says, that browser will
# refuse to reach this host over http at all, and there is no way to reach
# into it and shorten that. A day is long enough to be a real commitment and
# short enough that a mistake ages out by tomorrow.
#
# NO preload. Submitting to the preload list bakes this host into browser
# binaries, and getting back off takes months of release trains that nobody
# here controls. It is not a header you can retract.
#
# NO includeSubDomains. It would extend the promise to every subdomain,
# including ones that do not exist yet and were never checked for TLS.
#
# Raise max-age only after the setup has been proven stable on the deployed
# site over time, one step at a time. tests/headers.spec.ts asserts the
# ceiling and the two absent directives so none of this can be widened by
# accident. See README for the full reasoning.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-QzWFZi+FLIx23tnm9SBU4aEgx4x8DsuASP07mfqol/c=' 'sha256-Ya0pUYrC7nM5Cn/056TyVuEiz6dFGrzmkWzgON0pF0U='; style-src 'self' 'sha256-vv9IoKo7BSLbWcUHr3tNmfNVmm5L/9Cfn2H6LMk7/ow='; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
